        {
          "text": "WAN Ching 萬經 (T. 授一, H. 九沙, 小跛), Feb. 4, 1659-1741, Mar. 11, scholar and calligrapher, a native of Yin-hsien, Chekiang, was the son of Wan Ssŭ-ta and grandson of Wan T'ai [qq. v.]. He was brought up in Hangchow and later made his home there.",
